[Music]  back-to-school season means scouting  fashion inspiration if you're looking to  add some royal style to your look for  the new year check out these modern  princesses to get you started if this is  your first time here don't forget to hit  that subscribe button do you like making  crafts check out our friends over at  crafty hackers they'll show you how to  turn your everyday objects into awesome  things now let's find out what with  Disney Princesses look like as teens  [Music]  Rapunzel this drawing of a long-legged  Princess Rapunzel was created by Bev  Johnson Bev studied at the Rhode Island  School of Design she wanted to develop  casual versions of her favorite Disney  Princesses the illustration perfectly  captures Rapunzel's excited and curious  energy who are loving her relaxed and  girly style in a super cute dress and  comfy sweater her iconic hair hangs over  her shoulder in a thick braid adorned  with flowers we can't help but notice  that Rapunzel has definitely had a trim  in this depiction who was the choice to  shorten her hair merely to make the  character more realistic maybe the  artist is celebrating the freedom  Rapunzel finds from her controlling  captor either way this reimagining of  her puzzle is adorable snow white's this  version of Snow White is goals every  part of her look is making us drool  platform boots a double-slit skirt and a  tank top bring this princess to the  bleeding edge of fashion her full sleeve  tattoo pays homage to the princesses  roots her dark lip look and gorgeous  sunglasses  Linda grown-up and sultry tone and check  out those earrings but we're loving the  intrigue the fun kicks a haircut and  bold brows are on points Victoria Evans  has taken Snow White from the 1930s to  2018 flawlessly we are loving this edgy  look we need to talk about Tiana in this  sweetly ruffled Sun dress can you handle  how adorable this illustration is this  light sunny yellow is the perfect color  the playful ruffles soften a serious and  hardworking character and that kitschy  frog purse we're eating it up in The  Princess and the Frog Tiana is reserved  and goal driven we love her work ethic  and dedication to her goal  it's incredible to see this determined  character portrayed by Bev Johnson with  so much fun energy even her hair is  laid-back and simple her natural hair  beauty shines in this low-maintenance  but high style look Cinderella then  every piece of princess inspired artists  sweet Italian artist Emanuel V's visions  are a bit spicier his version of  Cinderella is a tattooed and pierced  pinup his work showcases the rebellious  and robust spirit in every princess  he's created a Cinderella who isn't  afraid to be herself who are loving the  green hair and the victory rolls a  septum ring leans and edgy but still  trendy tone this fierce rendering is a  beautiful contrast to the princess's  humble roots the artist has thoughtfully  included tattoos that honor her loyal  friends this girl won't be scrubbing  anyone's floors she's too busy being a  girl boss Jasmine Princess Jasmine is a  strong woman who thinks for herself she  refused to marry a prince and demanded  to marry for love we love her fierce  independence and adventurous spirit  artists and children's book illustrator  Anusha Syed has brought this independent  girl to the 21st century in her  illustration jasmine is a stylish travel  blogger Anushka sees jasmine with  accessories that express who she is her  friend Raja is honored with a killer  tiger print bag her harem pants are a  stylish nod to her Middle Eastern  heritage we loved the little detail of  the genie lamp on her cute tee jasmine  is still a cat lover the artist imagines  she has five at home mamako she's in  charge of every single day of my life  Merida who doesn't love wild girl Merida  her strong will and bravery made her a  fan favorite artist Bev Donson imagines  this fiery princess as a cute casual and  feisty team Merida's look is adorable  the hunter green of her button-down  complements her red mane we're loving  the denim shorts and stocking combo  paired with personal accessories this  look is effortless how cute is that belt  buckle or those tights we can barely  stand it we love that the artist didn't  try to tame Merida's wild hair she's  still the free spirit we all know and  love the only thing missing is a cute  arrow necklace Milan Milan is one of the  most essential Disney Princesses she  dared to obey her father and her culture  to save her country the real-life Mulan  was just as inspirational and became a  general Victoria Evans vision of the  courageous warrior captures her  willingness to ditch societal norms  artist Victoria Evans portrays Mulan as  healthy fit and sporty and perfectly  coordinated athletic wear her low  maintenance haircut and killer abs  demonstrate that Mulan lets nothing  distract her from her goals we love this  look for such a physically strong  character this illustration shows that  nothing looks as good as being true to  yourself though who doesn't love sweet  Belle this bookish daydreamer was  willing to sacrifice herself for her  father and even saw the good and beast  Val is a sincere and studious girl with  the heart of gold  this illustration of the bookworm beauty  by bev johnson is too cute for words her  simple ponytail and giant glasses  capture her humility her look is cozy  with an oversized cuddly sweater her  blue pen aphorism nod to her 16th  century wardrobe this comfy outfit makes  it easy to picture Belle curled up by a  fire with a good book for loving a cute  bow in her relaxed ponytail that was  adorable style would be the envy of any  bookworm  erielle fans of The Little Mermaid know  princes Ariel as the headstrong and less  an obedient daughter of King Triton half  of the film seems to be Ariel getting in  hot water not a saint art imagines the  ginger mermaid as a hip-hop loving gamer  girl  Ariel rocks diddums shorts in this  rendering her purple clam shells have  been replaced with a bot crop top Ariel  is comfortable being herself and chowing  down on pizza while she kicks back  playing video games were loving her wild  hair held back by a bulls cap Pocahontas  this progressive princess is stunning in  the portrayal of her as a college  student the artist imagines Pocahontas  uses her love of communication and  diplomacy as she studies linguistics the  silhouette of her dress is a throwback  to the original look of the character  her blue eyeshadow is a 100% modern  addition the cute compass tattoo on her  calf showcases her pioneering spirit and  of adventure Anusha sigh at imagine that  Pocahontas is still a thrill seeker  spending her free time hiking up  mountains and kayaking down Rapids we  love the faux raccoon tell on her bag  and the shell necklace the artist nails  the character in her adorable look we  hope you love these modern-day  princesses before you go don't forget to  check out our friends over at crafty  hackers if you love Disney you  absolutely have to check out their  videos on Disney inspired DIYs so you  can create some of these outfits at home  go give them a like for all their hard  work see you next time  [Music]  [Music]

